  {"id":"hi6_18","language":"html","difficulty":"intermediate","bug_type":"css","title":"CSS Variables for Theming","code":":root {\n  --color-primary: #0066cc;\n  --color-primary-hover: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-primary), black 15%);\n  --color-on-primary: white;\n}\n\n.btn-primary {\n  background: var(--color-primary);\n  color: var(--color-on-primary);\n}\n.btn-primary:hover {\n  background: var(--color-primary-hover);\n}","bugs":[]},
  {"id":"hi6_19","language":"html","difficulty":"intermediate","bug_type":"css","title":"Relative Color Syntax","code":".brand-light {\n  background: oklch(from var(--brand) l c h / 0.1);\n}","bugs":[]},
  {"id":"hi6_20","language":"html","difficulty":"intermediate","bug_type":"css","title":"Wide Color Gamut Display-P3","code">.vivid {\n  color: color(display-p3 1 0 0);\n  @supports not (color: color(display-p3 0 0 0)) {\n    color: rgb(255, 0, 0);\n  }\n}","bugs":[{"lines":[3],"fix":"@supports (color: color(display-p3 0 0 0)) {\n  .vivid { color: color(display-p3 1 0 0); }\n}","explanation":"The `@supports` rule checks if a feature is supported before using it, not after. Nesting a `@supports not` inside the block that already uses the feature is logically inverted. Wrap the wide-gamut rule in `@supports (color: color(display-p3 0 0 0))` and keep the fallback outside."}]}
